======================================================================
STEP 3: operational definition + conclusion
======================================================================
NEGLIGIBLE := the comparison whose up/down DEG balance does NOT reject
H0(p_up=0.5) in a two-sided exact binomial test at alpha=0.05 (no directional bias).
Across every DE threshold and both (independent/paired) models, 'Final vs Baseline
Blood' has the FEWEST DEGs and the MOST balanced up/down (closest to 50/50, highest
binomial p); it is the ONLY comparison that reaches a non-significant (balanced)
binomial test (|log2FC|>=2: 16 up vs 24 down, p=0.268). Both dentate-gyrus-vs-blood
comparisons are dominated by tissue-identity differences (thousands of DEGs, ~56-58%
up, p<=2e-49).

ANSWER: Final vs Baseline Blood shows negligible effects.
